ial role in the economic and cultural development of the Great Lakes region. With its strategic location at the head of Lake Erie and proximity to the Niagara River, Buffalo became a pivotal hub for trade and transportation, influencing the movement of goods across North America. Key figures in its development include local politicians and business leaders who harnessed its geographic advantages to foster growth and prosperity.

